Next-level roadmap (senior-style)
If booking + payments already work, you’re at a good “feature complete” stage. To push this project toward senior-level, focus on production readiness and operational excellence.
1) Reliability & failure handling
    -Add idempotency keys for booking/payment actions (prevent duplicate processing on retries).
    -Add retry-safe webhook handling (store processed Stripe event IDs, ignore duplicates).
    -Introduce state machine validation for booking statuses (prevent invalid transitions).
    -Add dead-letter / reconciliation job:
        -scan refund_pending
        -retry refunds
        -alert if still failing.
2) Observability (real-world critical)
    - Structured logging (JSON) with requestId, userId, bookingId, sessionId.
    - Metrics dashboard:
        - checkout success rate
        - webhook latency
        - refund rate
        - booking conflict rate
        - p95/p99 API latency.
    - Error monitoring (Sentry or similar) with release tracking.
3) Performance & load testing
    - Run load tests on key APIs:
        - GET /api/bookings/availability
        - POST /api/bookings/create-checkout-session
        - webhook endpoint burst simulation.
    - Tools: k6 (simple + popular) or Artillery.
    - Scenarios:
        - normal traffic (50–100 VUs)
        - peak burst (300+ VUs)
        - “same table/time” race tests.
    - Define SLO targets:
        - availability API p95 < 200ms
        - create session p95 < 500ms
        - <1% 5xx during peak.
    - Add indexes and caching based on bottlenecks found from tests.
4) Security hardening
    - Rate limit auth + booking endpoints.
    - Add strict input validation + schema validation on all routes.
    - Add Helmet/CSP and tighten CORS in prod.
    - Secret management (never plain .env in deployment).
    - Add audit logs for admin actions (who clicked Check In/No Show/Cancel and when).
5) Data & compliance quality
    - Add migration strategy/versioned schema updates.
    - Add backup/restore playbook and test restore drill.
    - Add data retention policy (messages/logs/payment metadata).
    - Build admin reconciliation report:
        -bookings vs Stripe charges vs refunds consistency.
6) Test strategy (senior signal)
    - Unit tests for booking rules/cost/refund logic.
    - Integration tests for API + DB constraints.
    - Contract tests for Stripe webhook payload handling.
    - E2E test for booking happy path and conflict/refund path.
    - CI gates:
        - lint + test + build required before merge.
7) DevOps / release maturity
    - Add CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions):
        - test matrix
        - build artifacts
        - deploy staging then production.
    - Add health checks/readiness checks.
    - Blue/green or rolling deployment strategy.
    - Feature flags for risky flows (booking/refund changes).
8) UX/business improvements (real ops value)
